@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Activities
+
+Activities describe changes to cards and comments across the boards you can access in an account.
+
+## `GET /:account_slug/activities.json`
+
+Returns a flat, [paginated](../README.md#pagination) array of activities, newest first. Follow the `Link` header with `rel="next"` to fetch subsequent pages. Activities are not grouped by day, and page sizes follow the API's dynamic pagination conventions.
+
+Only activity on boards accessible to the authenticated user is returned. Filters do not grant access to otherwise inaccessible boards or other accounts.
+
+### Filters
+
+| Parameter | Description |
+|-----------|-------------|
+| `creator_ids[]` | Limit activities to events created by these user IDs. This filters the event's creator, not the card's creator. |
+| `board_ids[]` | Limit activities to these board IDs. |
+
+Both filters accept multiple IDs. When both are supplied, an activity must match both filters.
+
+```bash
+curl --get \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer put-your-access-token-here" \
+  --data-urlencode "creator_ids[]=03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7" \
+  --data-urlencode "board_ids[]=03f5v9zjw8ri1g7h1udf8t18x" \
+  http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/686465299/activities.json
+```
+
+### Activity fields
+
+Each activity contains:
+
+| Field | Description |
+|-------|-------------|
+| `id` | The event's ID. |
+| `action` | The event's action, from the list below. |
+| `created_at` | When the event occurred, as an ISO 8601 timestamp in UTC. |
+| `description` | The event's plain-text description for the current user. |
+| `particulars` | Event-specific details, described below. Always an object. |
+| `url` | A browser URL opening the card. For comment events, it includes an anchor that jumps to the comment, such as `/686465299/cards/42#comment_03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7`. |
+| `eventable_type` | `Card` or `Comment`. |
+| `eventable` | The existing [card](cards.md) or [comment](comments.md) representation used by their list endpoints. |
+| `board` | The existing [board](boards.md) representation. |
+| `creator` | The existing [user](users.md) representation for the event's creator. |
+
+### Actions
+
+The feed includes the same kinds of events as the HTML timeline, except that it omits deprecated `card_collection_changed` events and includes `card_title_changed` events:
+
+- `card_assigned`
+- `card_unassigned`
+- `card_published`
+- `card_closed`
+- `card_reopened`
+- `card_board_changed`
+- `card_postponed`
+- `card_auto_postponed`
+- `card_title_changed`
+- `card_triaged`
+- `card_sent_back_to_triage`
+- `comment_created`
+
+### Particulars
+
+| Action | `particulars` fields |
+|--------|---------------------|
+| `card_assigned`, `card_unassigned` | `assignee_ids`: the IDs of the users assigned or unassigned. |
+| `card_board_changed` | `old_board`, `new_board`: the old and new board names. |
+| `card_title_changed` | `old_title`, `new_title`: the old and new card titles. |
+| `card_triaged` | `column`: the column name. |
+| All other actions | An empty object: `{}`. |
+
+Missing board names, titles, and column names are returned as empty strings (`""`), not `null`. Only the fields associated with the event's action are exposed. For example, a title change has:
+
+```json
+{
+  "old_title": "Fix the layout",
+  "new_title": "Fix the mobile layout"
+}
+```
